## Reliable timer implementation

Never rely only on a coroutine or a continuously decrementing variable to determine elapsed time.

Persist:

- Session ID.
- Start timestamp.
- Pause timestamp, if applicable.
- Accumulated paused duration.
- End timestamp.
- Status.
- Linked quest ID.
- Actual focused duration.

Derive elapsed time from timestamps and saved state.

Recover correctly after:

- Activity recreation.
- Screen rotation.
- App backgrounding.
- Process death.
- Device restart where practical.

Use lifecycle-aware observation and avoid unnecessarily running a permanent background service.

If a timer is active when the app returns to the foreground, reconstruct its state and show the correct remaining time.

Do not continue counting paused time as productive time.

